/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1191 0 R
/E (Active Mechanism: The intense peppery, bitter bite of arugula comes from glucosinolates \(specifically erucin and sulforaphane precursors\). Bitter compounds stimulate taste receptors on the tongue, triggering a vagal nerve reflex that commands the gallbladder to contract and release fresh bile. Bile acts like biological dish soap, emulsifying dietary fats and carrying neutralized toxins into the digestive tract for elimination.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
